Fri Nov 13 23:08:22 UTC 2026 - Caio César Ortega <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Add siag-pw-keyboard-focus.patch: PW only took keyboard input
  while the pointer was over its window. The shell's ChangeManaged
  makes the unrealized topbox its focus widget first, so Xt never
  selected KeyPress on the shell window and keys delivered there
  (click-to-focus, pointer elsewhere) were dropped. The focus is now
  cleared before activate_window() sets it to the text grid

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov 13 22:05:00 UTC 2026 - Caio César Ortega <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Add siag-pw-modified-flag.patch: in PW, ins_text() never set the
  buffer's modified flag, so typing (or pasting) text within a line
  left the document "unchanged" and File > Exit, Ctrl+Q or the window
  manager's close button quit without asking to save. Files given on
  the command line are now marked unmodified after loading

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov 13 21:20:25 UTC 2026 - Caio César Ortega <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Add siag-form-dialog-focus.patch: form dialogs (File > Print
  Format, Tools > Environment > Custom, ...) warped the pointer to
  their corner before the window manager placed them, so it jumped to
  the middle of the screen; the warp is gone. The dialog now carries
  _NET_WM_USER_TIME so xfwm4's focus-stealing prevention gives it the
  focus, and WM_DELETE_WINDOW so the window manager's close button
  cancels the form instead of killing the program
- Add siag-print-format-save.patch: File > Print Format opened with
  empty fields and only changed the commands for the session, and
  load-applications was an empty stub, so ~/.siag/applications.sh was
  written but never read. The form now shows the current previewer and
  print commands, saves them, and they are loaded at start-up. One
  shared print-format in common.scm also fixes Egon's menu entry,
  which called an undefined function

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov 13 19:19:07 UTC 2026 - Caio César Ortega <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Add siag-xedplus-delete-key.patch: Xedplus bound Delete and KP_Delete to delete-previous-character in both insert and overwrite modes, so Delete erased backwards like BackSpace; they now delete the next character (Meta+Delete deletes the next word). Matches the XawM fix for dialog text fields

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov 13 19:06:19 UTC 2026 - caiocco <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Add siag-selection-utf8.patch: text pasted from other programs
  showed accents as "Ã©" because their UTF-8 was inserted as Latin-1;
  siag and pw now ask for UTF8_STRING (falling back to STRING, also
  decoded when it is UTF-8) and convert to Latin-1, and offer
  UTF8_STRING and STRING when copying. Fix the reversed memcpy that
  left siag's TARGETS reply uninitialized. pw now rebreaks pasted
  paragraphs to the margins instead of leaving one long line past
  the right margin. Needs the matching Mowitz update

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov 13 17:40:00 UTC 2026 - caiocco <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Add siag-buffer-name-latin1.patch: buffer names came straight from
  UTF-8 file names, but lists, tabs and prompts draw Latin-1, so
  "ação.siag" showed as "aÃ§Ã£o.siag" (e.g. Close Buffer on exit).
  buffer_name() in siag, pw and egon now converts to Latin-1 (paths
  stay in the file system encoding); window titles are converted
  back to the locale encoding for Xt

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov 13 16:53:20 UTC 2026 - caiocco <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Add siag-pointer-cursors.patch: plus pointer over the spreadsheet
  grid (the motion handler reset it to None), I-beam over the edit
  line, cell editor and the pw page

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov 13 15:52:40 UTC 2026 - caiocco <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Add siag-xim-latin1.patch: the spreadsheet read keys with
  XLookupString, which does not compose dead keys; use Mowitz's
  MwLookupLatin1() so accented letters can be typed

